body:
Review findings addressed in a9b2d8a:
1. ring-cut levels are now detected from the program's shape (a real cut level with no fitted arc) and must carry their named note, and a named level must post no arc;
2. under Adaptive, wrap_exit caps each arc chord at 4 deg of turn (plus sagitta) and trims arc end chords to 0.01 mm: world program breaks past 5 deg on planned levels 12,824 -> 0, world moves 98,525 -> 160,989; OffsetRings output unchanged (digest);
3. a hard planner error on the wrap falls back to Offset rings for that level with a named note (no fixture reaches it cheaply - untested);
4. wrap tally note names the developed radius;
5. rings digest rounds to 1e-6 before hashing (new pin (5263, 11592310142122113043); the old bitwise digest still passed on the same build);
6. provenance line on the test file.
Tests: rotary_adaptive debug + release --ignored (2 passed, 122 s), rotary 10, lib machining3d 4, app rotary_verify 9 / rotary_fixtures 4 / golden_cl 23, clippy -D warnings clean.
